window.SPL_SEARCH_INDEX = [{"title":"Reliable AI workflows in native Python","page":"Introduction","href":"index.html","text":"Semantic Prompt Language v2 (SPL2) is a syntactic superset of Python for building reliable LLM and agentic workflows with typed schemas, dynamic prompt constraints, and deterministic capability sandboxing.","group":"Start here"},{"title":"Why SPL2?","page":"Introduction","href":"index.html#why-spl2","text":"","group":"Start here"},{"title":"How the Pipeline Works","page":"Introduction","href":"index.html#how-the-pipeline-works","text":"","group":"Start here"},{"title":"Where Next","page":"Introduction","href":"index.html#where-next","text":"","group":"Start here"},{"title":"Getting started with SPL2","page":"Getting started","href":"getting-started.html","text":"Install the spl2 runtime, configure your OpenAI or OpenAI-compatible endpoint, and run your first .spl2 workflow in under two minutes.","group":"Start here"},{"title":"Installation","page":"Getting started","href":"getting-started.html#installation","text":"Install the spl2 package from the lang directory using pip: Verify that the spl2 CLI is available:","group":"Start here"},{"title":"Provider Configuration","page":"Getting started","href":"getting-started.html#provider-configuration","text":"SPL2 uses the official openai Python SDK (Responses API and Structured Outputs) and works with OpenAI as well as any OpenAI-compatible provider: Variable Description --- --- OPENAI_API_KEY API key used for OpenAI Responses API calls OPENAI_BASE_URL Optional custom endpoint URL for OpenAI-compatible providers OPENAI_MODEL / SPL2_MODEL Default model when neither --model nor model= is specified SPL2_SEARCH_URL Optional DuckDuckGo HTML endpoint override for web_search Model selection follows strict precedence: CLI --model > per-call model= modifier > OPENAI_MODEL / SPL2_MODEL environment variable > default model (gpt-4.1).","group":"Start here","signatures":["OPENAI_API_KEY","OPENAI_BASE_URL","OPENAI_MODEL","SPL2_MODEL","SPL2_SEARCH_URL"]},{"title":"Your First Script","page":"Getting started","href":"getting-started.html#your-first-script","text":"Create a file named hello_ask.spl2: Validate syntax and modifiers statically without making any API calls: Inspect the transpiled Python code: Run the script with durable trace caching enabled: Standard print() output is routed to stderr, while stdout emits the structured JSON result envelope:","group":"Start here"},{"title":"The SPL2 Language","page":"Language","href":"language.html","text":"SPL2 is a true syntactic superset of Python 3.10+. Every valid Python construct—classes, decorators, list comprehensions, try/except, type annotations, and async/await—works unchanged inside .spl2 files.","group":"The language"},{"title":"Contextual Soft Keywords","page":"Language","href":"language.html#contextual-soft-keywords","text":"SPL2 introduces eight contextual (soft) keywords: Keyword Role Syntactic Form --- --- --- ask Single-turn, tool-free LLM call ask(...) \u003cprompt> or ask \u003cprompt> agent Autonomous tool-calling loop agent(...) \u003cprompt> or agent \u003cprompt> decide Boolean natural-language predicate decide(...) \u003cprompt> or decide \u003cprompt> enforce Scoped positive LLM instruction enforce \u003cexpr>: forbid Scoped negative LLM instruction forbid \u003cexpr>: restrict Scoped capability sandbox restrict(fs=..., net=..., exec=..., mcp=...): success Immediate \"ok\" termination success \u003cexpr> failure Immediate \"failure\" termination failure \u003cexpr> Because these keywords are contextual (like Python's match and case), they remain valid variable, parameter, function, and attribute names everywhere else:","group":"The language","signatures":["ask","agent","decide","enforce","forbid","restrict","success","failure"]},{"title":"Prompt Expressions & Strings","page":"Language","href":"language.html#prompt-expressions--strings","text":"ask, agent, decide, enforce, and forbid accept any Python string literal as well as any parenthesized or variable expression evaluating to a str:","group":"The language"},{"title":"Concurrency & async Support","page":"Language","href":"language.html#concurrency--async-support","text":"ask, agent, and decide work both synchronously and asynchronously:","group":"The language"},{"title":"Importing .spl2 and Python Modules","page":"Language","href":"language.html#importing-spl2-and-python-modules","text":"SPL2 registers importlib.abc.MetaPathFinder and SourceLoader hooks when launched via spl2:","group":"The language"},{"title":"Built-in Tools Library","page":"Language","href":"language.html#built-in-tools-library","text":"The five built-in agent tools can also be imported and called deterministically from .spl2 code:","group":"The language"},{"title":"LLM & Agent Calls","page":"LLM & Agent calls","href":"llm-commands.html","text":"SPL2 provides three specialized LLM execution keywords—ask, agent, and decide—backed by the OpenAI Responses API, Pydantic Structured Outputs, built-in tools, and Model Context Protocol (MCP) servers.","group":"The language"},{"title":"Modifiers Reference","page":"LLM & Agent calls","href":"llm-commands.html#modifiers-reference","text":"ask, agent, and decide accept optional keyword modifiers inside parentheses: Modifier Applies To Type / Values Description --- --- --- --- len ask , agent , decide 'word' \\ 'sentence' \\ 'paragraph' \\ 'long' or str System prompt guidance instructing target response length fmt ask , agent , decide 'text' \\ 'object' \\ 'array' \\ 'string' \\ 'float' \\ 'int' \\ 'bool' Output format validation and parsing (mutually exclusive with schema ) schema ask , agent , decide type[BaseModel] or TypeAdapter type Validates and parses JSON output into a typed Python/Pydantic instance tokens ask , agent , decide int > 0 Hard output token limit ( max_output_tokens ) retries ask , agent , decide int >= 0 (default 0 ) Self-repair retries on validation error and exponential backoff on transient API errors thinking ask , agent , decide 'none' \\ 'low' \\ 'medium' \\ 'high' \\ 'max' Reasoning effort mapped to OpenAI reasoning configuration files ask , agent , decide str \\ Path \\ Sequence[str \\ Path] Attaches UTF-8 text ( \u003cfile> ), images ( input_image ), and PDFs ( input_file ) model ask , agent , decide str Per-call model override data decide Any Structured evidence serialized into the predicate prompt tools agent only Sequence[str] or comma-separated str Allowlist of built-in tools enabled for this agent call mcp agent only str \\ Sequence[str] Allowlist of MCP servers/tools ( \"server\" , \"server/*\" , or \"server/tool\" ) max_steps agent only int > 0 (default 25 ) Maximum tool-calling turns in the agent loop","group":"The language","signatures":["len","fmt","schema","tokens","retries","thinking","files","model","data","tools","mcp","max_steps"]},{"title":"ask — Single-Turn LLM Calls","page":"LLM & Agent calls","href":"llm-commands.html#ask--single-turn-llm-calls","text":"ask executes a single-turn, tool-free LLM call. When schema= or fmt= is provided, the response is validated and parsed automatically; if validation fails and retries > 0, SPL2 feeds the validation error back to the model for self-repair.","group":"The language"},{"title":"agent — Autonomous Tool Loops & MCP","page":"LLM & Agent calls","href":"llm-commands.html#agent--autonomous-tool-loops--mcp","text":"agent runs an autonomous tool-calling loop bounded by max_steps (default 25). By default, agents have access to five built-in tools:","group":"The language"},{"title":"MCP Configuration","page":"LLM & Agent calls","href":"llm-commands.html#mcp-configuration","text":"Configure local (stdio) and remote (http / sse) MCP servers via --mcp \u003cconfig.json> or .mcp.json in the working directory:","group":"The language"},{"title":"decide — Boolean Predicate Evaluation","page":"LLM & Agent calls","href":"llm-commands.html#decide--boolean-predicate-evaluation","text":"decide evaluates a natural-language predicate against optional structured data= evidence and returns a Python bool (True or False):","group":"The language"},{"title":"Policies, Sandboxing & Termination","page":"Policies & sandboxing","href":"safety.html","text":"SPL2 separates prompt-level guidance (enforce, forbid) from deterministic runtime capability sandboxing (restrict) and guarantees a single JSON output envelope on stdout (success, failure).","group":"The language"},{"title":"enforce & forbid","page":"Policies & sandboxing","href":"safety.html#enforce--forbid","text":"enforce \u003cexpr>: and forbid \u003cexpr>: dynamically scope mandatory positive and negative instructions across all nested ask, agent, and decide calls:","group":"The language"},{"title":"restrict Capability Sandboxing","page":"Policies & sandboxing","href":"safety.html#restrict-capability-sandboxing","text":"restrict(fs=..., net=..., exec=..., mcp=...): enforces deterministic guardrails on built-in tools and agent tool calls within the block: Modifier Guardrail --- --- fs Canonical path containment for read_file , write_file , and files= attachments net Allowed hostnames or wildcard domains ( *.example.com ) for web_fetch and web_search exec Allowed executable names for shell (such as 'git,pytest' ) mcp Allowed MCP servers/tools ( \"server\" , \"server/*\" , or \"server/tool\" )","group":"The language","signatures":["fs","net","exec","mcp"]},{"title":"Nested Intersection Semantics","page":"Policies & sandboxing","href":"safety.html#nested-intersection-semantics","text":"When restrict blocks are nested, their allowlists are intersected—inner blocks can only narrow permissions, never widen them: Because enforce, forbid, and restrict are stored in contextvars.ContextVar, constraints apply across helper functions, ThreadPoolExecutor workers, and concurrent asyncio.gather() tasks without cross-task bleed.","group":"The language"},{"title":"success, failure & Output Contract","page":"Policies & sandboxing","href":"safety.html#success-failure--output-contract","text":"Every SPL2 execution emits a single structured JSON envelope on stdout: or on failure (exiting with a non-zero exit code):","group":"The language"},{"title":"CLI & Runtime Reference","page":"CLI & runtime","href":"cli.html","text":"The spl2 CLI compiles, lints, traces, and executes .spl2 scripts with built-in record-and-replay caching and a live Textual terminal UI.","group":"Reference"},{"title":"Command-Line Synopsis","page":"CLI & runtime","href":"cli.html#command-line-synopsis","text":"All [script_args...] following \u003cscript.spl2> are forwarded into standard Python sys.argv. Flag Description --- --- --check Run static lint and AST validation without executing the script or requiring an API key ( 0 on valid, 1 on errors) --emit-py Output the transpiled Python source code (preserving original line numbers) to stdout --model \u003cname> Override the OpenAI model for all calls in the run (highest precedence) --mcp \u003cconfig.json> Load MCP server definitions from \u003cconfig.json> (defaults to .mcp.json if present) --trace [file] Enable durable record-and-replay caching (defaults to \u003cscript_name>.trace.jsonl ) --log \u003clevel> Set stderr logging level ( DEBUG , INFO , WARNING , ERROR ) --realtime Launch the live Textual TUI on stderr with real-time token and tool streaming","group":"Reference","signatures":["--check","--emit-py","--model \u003cname>","--mcp \u003cconfig.json>","--trace [file]","--log \u003clevel>","--realtime"]},{"title":"Caching & Replay (--trace)","page":"CLI & runtime","href":"cli.html#caching--replay---trace","text":"Passing --trace records all ask, decide, agent, MCP, and deterministic tool calls as append-only JSONL entries:","group":"Reference"},{"title":"Live Terminal UI (--realtime)","page":"CLI & runtime","href":"cli.html#live-terminal-ui---realtime","text":"Running with --realtime launches an interactive Textual terminal UI rendered to stderr:","group":"Reference"},{"title":"VS Code Extension","page":"CLI & runtime","href":"cli.html#vs-code-extension","text":"The SPL2 VS Code extension in vscode/ provides:","group":"Reference"},{"title":"Grammar & Compile-Time Lint Rules","page":"Grammar & lint rules","href":"grammar.html","text":"SPL2 extends the Python 3.10+ grammar with contextual keyword productions processed by a token-stream mapper (tokenize) and validated by an AST linter (ast.NodeVisitor).","group":"Reference"},{"title":"EBNF Grammar Extensions","page":"Grammar & lint rules","href":"grammar.html#ebnf-grammar-extensions","text":"","group":"Reference"},{"title":"Compile-Time Lint Rules","page":"Grammar & lint rules","href":"grammar.html#compile-time-lint-rules","text":"Both spl2 --check and normal execution enforce six static lint rules before any code runs, formatting diagnostics with filename, line, column, source snippet, and caret pointer: Example lint output:","group":"Reference"},{"title":"End-to-End Examples","page":"Examples","href":"examples.html","text":"Explore complete .spl2 scripts combining Pydantic structured outputs, autonomous agents, capability restrictions, boolean decisions, and asyncio concurrency.","group":"Guides"},{"title":"Structured Extraction with Pydantic","page":"Examples","href":"examples.html#structured-extraction-with-pydantic","text":"","group":"Guides"},{"title":"Sandboxed Repository Agent","page":"Examples","href":"examples.html#sandboxed-repository-agent","text":"","group":"Guides"},{"title":"Scoped Constraints & Boolean Decision Guard","page":"Examples","href":"examples.html#scoped-constraints--boolean-decision-guard","text":"","group":"Guides"},{"title":"Concurrent async / await Tasks with Isolated Contexts","page":"Examples","href":"examples.html#concurrent-async--await-tasks-with-isolated-contexts","text":"","group":"Guides"}];
